 ### Dynamic tool calls (experimental)
 
+#### Local execution allowlist (Benchline candidate patch)
+
+The Benchline candidate adds `features.tool_registry.execution_allowlist`, an
+exact namespace-to-tool-name map. Omission preserves the upstream default; an
+empty map denies every model tool. Plain function names use `functions`.
+For example, a client that supplies three mediated dynamic tools can use:
+
+```toml
+[features.tool_registry.execution_allowlist]
+functions = ["exec", "wait", "benchline_prepare_action", "benchline_action_status", "benchline_execute_action"]
+```
+
+The registry omits other tools from direct and Code Mode definitions and rejects
+their dispatch before hooks or handlers, including forged direct and nested
+calls. Code Mode's `exec` and `wait` also need explicit admission. Provider-hosted
+tools are disabled whenever this restriction is present because they do not
+execute through the local dispatcher. It does not grant permission, constrain
+explicit client-originated app-server RPCs, or replace the client's action gate,
+process isolation, configuration ownership, approval checks or output handling.
+The host must pin and validate this configuration; do not expose configuration
+overrides or arbitrary app-server RPCs to the model. This local patch is not an
+upstream-supported configuration option.
+
 `dynamicTools` on `thread/start` and the corresponding `item/tool/call` request/response flow are experimental APIs. To enable them, set `initialize.params.capabilities.experimentalApi = true`.
 
 Each entry in `dynamicTools` is either a top-level function or a namespace containing function tools. Dynamic tool identifiers follow the same constraints as Responses tools:
